-- examples/checks/holes-negation-unknown.rofl — `unknown(A)` OF WHAT A HOLE
-- LEFT OUT IS A SHRUG, under the default semantics, in both engines
-- (docs/aggregates.md, "Shrugs, as built"; it replaced the refusal of
-- f_unknown_beside_a_hole_was_guarded_only_under_well_founded). c's win would
-- hold if B + 1 had a value; 2^60 is past the range, so hu_win(c) is left
-- out, and `not unknown(hu_win(c))` is no answer, never hu_decided(c). k's win
-- holds, so its question is decided.
edb(hu_big).
edb(hu_pos).
hu_big(1152921504606846975).
hu_pos(c). hu_pos(k).
hu_win(k).
hu_win(c) :- hu_big(B), Z is B + 1, Z > 0.
hu_decided(X) :- hu_pos(X), not unknown(hu_win(X)).
